'''''Aglaonema commutatum''''', the '''poison dart plant''', is a species of flowering plant in the Chinese evergreen genus ''[[Aglaonema]]'', family [[Araceae]]. It is native to the Philippines and northeastern [[Sulawesi]], and has been introduced to other tropical locales, including Cuba, Puerto Rico, Trinidad and Tobago, Comoros, the [[Chagos Archipelago]], India, Bangladesh, and the [[Cook Islands]].<ref name="84050-1" >{{cite web |url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:84050-1 |title=''Aglaonema commutatum'' Schott |author=<!--Not stated--> |website=Plants of the World Online |publisher=Board of Trustees of the Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew |access-date=12 October 2021 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=''Aglaonema commutatum'' poison dart plant |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/703/aglaonema-commutatum/details |date=2021 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=12 October 2021 }}</ref> Its hybrid cultivar 'Silver Queen' (with ''[[Aglaonema nitidum|A. nitidum]]'') has gained the [[Royal Horticultural Society]]'s [[Award of Garden Merit]] as a houseplant.<ref>{{cite web |title=''Aglaonema commutatum'' 'Silver Queen' Chinese evergreen 'Silver Queen' |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/92017/aglaonema-silver-queen/details |date=2021 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=12 October 2021 |quote=Synonyms; ''Aglaonema treubyi'' 'Silver Queen', ''Aglaonema commutatum'' 'Silver Queen', ''Aglaonema nitidum'' 'Silver Queen' }}</ref>

==Subtaxa==
The following varieties are accepted:<ref name="84050-1" />
*''Aglaonema commutatum'' var. ''commutatum'' – central Luzon
*''Aglaonema commutatum'' var. ''elegans'' {{small|(Engl.) Nicolson}} – central Luzon
*''Aglaonema commutatum'' var. ''maculatum'' {{small|(Hook.f.) Nicolson}} – central Luzon
*''Aglaonema commutatum'' var. ''warburgii'' {{small|(Engl.) Nicolson}} – northeast Sulawesi
